<?php $activity=$transactionalActivity;$stateLabels=['queued'=>'Queued / retrying','processing'=>'Processing','accepted'=>'Transport accepted','failed'=>'Failed','uncertain'=>'Acceptance uncertain','cancelled'=>'Cancelled','development'=>'Development only']; ?>
<section class="transactional-intro"><div><p class="transactional-eyebrow">APPLICATION EMAIL</p><h2>Reach connections when an action calls for it</h2><p>Track the operational emails MOED already creates: signup confirmations, Inbox replies and notifications, account access, task digests, engagement correspondence, and reimbursement submissions.</p><p>These are separate from campaign and audience automation. MOED generates each message from the action that requires it.</p><div class="audience-actions"><a class="audience-button" href="<?= $h($url(['view'=>'delivery'])) ?>">Email delivery settings</a><a href="#transactional-activity">View activity ↓</a></div></div><ol class="transactional-path" aria-label="Transactional email lifecycle"><li><?= audienceFlowIcon('trigger') ?><span>MOED action</span><small>Signup, recovery, correspondence</small></li><li><?= audienceFlowIcon('archive') ?><span>Queued for delivery</span><small>Durable attempt and status tracking</small></li><li><?= audienceFlowIcon('email') ?><span>Configured transport</span><small>SES or MOED’s SMTP transport</small></li><li><?= audienceFlowIcon('status') ?><span>Acceptance recorded</span><small>Acceptance does not prove inbox delivery</small></li></ol></section>
<section class="transactional-readiness" aria-label="Sending readiness"><div><h2>MessageMonkey sending gate</h2><strong><?= !$sesStatus||!$sesStatus['production_access']||!$bulkApproved?'Live campaign sending remains gated':'See delivery settings for current qualification' ?></strong><p><?php if($sesStatus&&$sesStatus['region']!==''): ?>Stored SES snapshot: <?= $h($sesStatus['region']) ?> · Production access <?= $sesStatus['production_access']?'enabled':'not enabled' ?> · SES sending <?= $sesStatus['sending_enabled']?'enabled':'disabled' ?>. Last check: <?= $h($sesStatus['checked_at']?:'not yet checked') ?><?php else: ?>SES is not configured for this audience.<?php endif; ?></p></div><p>Signup-confirmation emails keep their existing SES readiness requirements. MOED’s operational SMTP queues keep their existing policies. Viewing this page does not send, retry, or enable email.</p></section>
<section id="transactional-activity"><div class="section-title"><h2>Recent transactional activity</h2><a href="<?= $h($url(['view'=>'transactional']+$transactionalFilters)) ?>">Refresh activity</a></div>
<form class="flow-list-filters" method="get"><?php audienceInputs(['view'=>'transactional']); ?><label>Time window<select name="days"><?php foreach([7,30,90]as$days): ?><option value="<?= $days ?>"<?= $days===$transactionalFilters['days']?' selected':'' ?>>Last <?= $days ?> days</option><?php endforeach; ?></select></label><label>Email source<select name="source"><option value="">All sources</option><?php foreach($transactionalSources as$key=>$source): ?><option value="<?= $key ?>"<?= $key===$transactionalFilters['source']?' selected':'' ?>><?= $h($source['label']) ?></option><?php endforeach; ?></select></label><label>Status<select name="state"><option value="">All statuses</option><?php foreach($stateLabels as$key=>$label): ?><option value="<?= $key ?>"<?= $key===$transactionalFilters['state']?' selected':'' ?>><?= $label ?></option><?php endforeach; ?></select></label><button>Apply</button></form>
<div class="transactional-totals" aria-label="Status totals for selected sources and time window"><?php foreach(['queued','accepted','failed','uncertain']as$state): ?><article><h3><?= $stateLabels[$state] ?></h3><strong><?= number_format($activity['totals'][$state]??0) ?></strong></article><?php endforeach; ?></div>
<?php if($activity['unavailable']): ?><p class="audience-notice">Activity is unavailable for: <?= $h(implode(', ',$activity['unavailable'])) ?>. These queues require their database update; they are not included in totals.</p><?php endif; ?>
<div class="audience-table-scroll"><table class="data-table transactional-activity-table"><thead><tr><th>Created (UTC)</th><th>Email source</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Queue status</th><th>Attempts</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach($activity['rows']as$row): ?><tr><td><time><?= $h(substr($row['created_at'],0,19)) ?></time></td><td><?= $h($transactionalSources[$row['source']]['label']) ?><small class="transactional-transport"><?= $h($transactionalSources[$row['source']]['transport']) ?><?php if($row['id']!==null): ?> · #<?= (int)$row['id'] ?><?php endif; ?></small></td><td><?= $h(ucfirst(str_replace('_',' ',$row['purpose']))) ?></td><td><span class="transactional-state state-<?= $h($row['state']) ?>"><?= $h($stateLabels[$row['state']]??$row['state']) ?></span></td><td><?= $row['attempts']===null?'—':(int)$row['attempts'] ?></td></tr><?php endforeach; ?><?php if(!$activity['rows']): ?><tr><td colspan="5">No transactional activity matches these filters.</td></tr><?php endif; ?></tbody></table></div>
<nav class="audience-pagination" aria-label="Transactional activity pages"><span><?= number_format($activity['total']) ?> records</span><div><?php if($activity['page']>1): ?><a aria-label="Previous page" href="<?= $h($url(array_replace(['view'=>'transactional'],$transactionalFilters,['page'=>$activity['page']-1]))) ?>">←</a><?php endif; ?><span><?= $activity['page'] ?> / <?= $activity['pages'] ?></span><?php if($activity['page']<$activity['pages']): ?><a aria-label="Next page" href="<?= $h($url(array_replace(['view'=>'transactional'],$transactionalFilters,['page'=>$activity['page']+1]))) ?>">→</a><?php endif; ?></div></nav>
<p class="audience-help">Transport accepted means SES or SMTP accepted the message for further delivery. Uncertain acceptance requires review before retrying to avoid duplicates. Attempt counts are unavailable for access emails and digests under the existing permissions. This view contains queue metadata only; message contents, recipients, access links, and transport errors are not exposed here.</p></section>
<details class="flow-native-scope"><summary>How this maps to Mailchimp Transactional</summary><p>Mailchimp Transactional is a separate developer API/SMTP product. MessageMonkey currently uses MOED’s existing application events and encrypted queues. A public sending API, separate SMTP gateway, vendor billing, and imported Mandrill templates are not implemented.</p><p>Use <a href="<?= $h($url(['view'=>'flow-templates'])) ?>">Flow templates</a> for audience journeys and <a href="<?= $h($url(['view'=>'templates'])) ?>">Email templates</a> for marketing designs. System-email content remains managed by the corresponding MOED feature.</p></details>
